  "details": "Sometimes, a world will say it is PC/Quest, as in, there will be a quest uploaded version. However, this doesn't mean that the world is actually quest compatible. Some worlds instantly crash quest users upon entry, some worlds freeze the game when looking in a certain direction, and some worlds even crash the game on the load screen. A world uploader without a quest headset might be unaware of these issues. \n\nIt would be useful if quest users could have a 'report not quest compatible' option after an attempt to load the world that could be visible to the world creator, so they could get that feedback. It could be on the world page with the join button and description, and again, it would only be made available once a user has clicked the join button on that version of the world (after an update to the world is uploaded to quest, the user would have to attempt to join again before getting the report option). The reports/report count doesn't have to be visible to users, just a notifier for the world creator. \n\nThe report could have a section of feedback text, or it could just be a counter similar to a likes counter. If there was an option for the user to identify their headset as quest 2 or quest 3 that would also be useful feedback (some worlds are only quest 2 crashers, as quest 3 and 3s have better specs).",
